request@5dc35465
  the slot is reserved at request time and travels in the event, so the reply writes a parameter key; a computed key would leave the invariants unproven
  one request per source at a time keeps the public APIs from being hammered by a button-masher
  the 5-second cooldown is politeness toward free APIs with no key; 5 is a guess, not a published limit
store@9ba1bdfe
  the reply carries src and slot back from the event, so one definition serves every source
give_up@dd413476
  a dropped reply would otherwise leave the source pending forever (the host has no request timeout)
upvote@057c3699
  votes are anonymous: Kern has no identity for page visitors yet, so one person can vote many times
